"original_id":"ap360","type":"person","label":"Charles Baudelaire","name_native":"","nationality":"","birth_year":null,"death_year":null,"image_url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/l449YMnPI9TesjFydVwDsNtGo14.jpg","is_phantom":true,"is_enriched":false,"hop_distance":3},{"id":"person_ap368","original_id":"ap368","type":"person","label":"Paul Durand-Ruel","name_native":"","nationality":"","birth_year":null,"death_year":null,"image_url":"","is_phantom":true,"is_enriched":false,"hop_distance":3},{"id":"person_ap369","original_id":"ap369","type":"person","label":"The Parisian Bourgeoisie","name_native":"","nationality":"","birth_year":null,"death_year":null,"image_url":"","is_phantom":true,"is_enriched":false,"hop_distance":3},{"id":"person_ap370","original_id":"ap370","type":"person","label":"Parisian Bourgeoisie","name_native":"","nationality":"","birth_year":null,"death_year":null,"image_url":"","is_phantom":true,"is_enriched":false,"hop_distance":3},{"id":"person_ap65","original_id":"ap65","type":"person","label":"Georges Clemenceau","name_native":"","nationality":"","birth_year":null,"death_year":null,"image_url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/xLB1KKa3GfOChIgQMesNEFgDavQ.jpg","is_phantom":true,"is_enriched":false,"hop_distance":3}],"edges":[{"source":"work_aw12","target":"person_ap6","type":"work_person","role_type":"artist","role_detail":"Artist"},{"source":"work_aw12","target":"work_aw41","type":"work_work","relation_type":"influenced","relation_note":"Monet's late paintings, where forms dissolve into shimmering fields of color, are often cited as precursors to Abstract Expressionism. Rothko's large canvases, which use color to evoke profound emotional and spiritual states, can be seen as a conceptual extension of Monet's late-career focus on pure chromatic and light effects."},{"source":"work_aw12","target":"work_aw51","type":"work_work","relation_type":"influenced","relation_note":"While created slightly before, Monet's late works, including the Venice series, pushed color into expressive, non-naturalistic realms that were central to the Fauvist movement, of which Derain was a key figure. Both artists used color to build form and convey emotion, liberating it from purely descriptive duty."},{"source":"work_aw12","target":"work_aw37","type":"work_work","relation_type":"inspired_by","relation_note":"Like many Impressionists, Monet was influenced by Japanese Ukiyo-e prints. Hokusai's series, depicting a single subject under various conditions, provided a conceptual model for Monet's own serial paintings, including his views of San Giorgio Maggiore."},{"source":"work_aw12","target":"work_aw49","type":"work_work","relation_type":"inspired_by","relation_note":"Monet greatly admired Turner's atmospheric depictions of Venice. Turner's focus on dissolving form into light and color, particularly over water, is a direct precedent for Monet's approach in his own Venetian series."},{"source":"work_aw12","target":"work_aw50","type":"work_work","relation_type":"inspired_by","relation_note":"Whistler's 'Nocturnes' explored tonal harmonies and capturing twilight moods, prioritizing atmosphere over detail. Monet's choice to paint San Giorgio Maggiore at dusk echoes Whistler's aesthetic of capturing the ephemeral moments between day and night."},{"source":"person_ap6","target":"person_ap64","type":"person_person","relation_type":"influenced_by","relation_note":"Derived: Water Lilies (Grandes Decorations) → On the Beach at Trouville","confidence":"corroborated"},{"source":"person_ap6","target":"person_ap74","type":"person_person","relation_type":"influenced_by","relation_note":"Derived: Water Lilies → The Great Wave off Kanagawa","confidence":"corroborated"},{"source":"person_ap71","target":"person_ap6","type":"person_person","relation_type":"influenced_by","relation_note":"Derived: Impression, Sunrise → The Starry Night","confidence":"corroborated"},{"source":"person_ap67","target":"person_ap6","type":"person_person","relation_type":"influenced_by","relation_note":"Derived: The Harvest → Water Lilies (Grandes Decorations)","confidence":"corroborated"},{"source":"person_ap6","target":"work_aw364","type":"person_work","role_type":"artist","role_detail":""},{"source":"person_ap6","target":"work_aw261","type":"person_work","role_type":"artist","role_detail":""},{"source":"person_ap6","target":"work_aw22","type":"person_work","role_type":"collaborator","role_detail":"Protégé"},{"source":"person_ap6","target":"work_aw110","type":"person_work","role_type":"artist","role_detail":"Artist"},{"source":"person_ap6","target":"work_aw8","type":"person_work","role_type":"artist","role_detail":"Artist"},{"source":"person_ap64","target":"work_aw109","type":"person_work","role_type":"artist","role_detail":"Artist"},{"source":"person_ap74","target":"work_aw23","type":"person_work","role_type":"artist","role_detail":""},{"source":"person_ap71","target":"work_aw355","type":"person_work","role_type":"artist","role_detail":"Artist"},{"source":"person_ap67","target":"work_aw111","type":"person_work","role_type":"artist","role_detail":"Artist"},{"source":"work_aw364","target":"person_ap6","type":"work_person","role_type":"artist","role_detail":""},{"source":"work_aw261","target":"person_ap6","type":"work_person","role_type":"artist","role_detail":""},{"source":"work_aw22","target":"person_ap354","type":"work_person","role_type":"artist","role_detail":"Artist"},{"source":"work_aw22","target":"person_ap355","type":"work_person","role_type":"subject","role_detail":"Subject"},{"source":"work_aw22","target":"person_ap356","type":"work_person","role_type":"subject","role_detail":"Subject"},{"source":"work_aw22","target":"person_ap359","type":"work_person","role_type":"subject","role_detail":"Subject"},{"source":"work_aw22","target":"person_ap360","type":"work_person","role_type":"collaborator","role_detail":"Advocate"},{"source":"work_aw22","target":"person_ap6","type":"work_person","role_type":"collaborator","role_detail":"Proté